# Neu hinzugekommen / newly added
L[cfg_saved]="The settings were saved and are active."
L[doc_title]="Updating a container"
L[doc_intro]="Updates are not installed from the browser but on the Proxmox host with this command. ID is the container number, for example 104. The container must be running."
L[doc_steps]="The command runs these steps in order:"
L[doc_step1]="Snapshot: if UPDATE_SNAPSHOT is enabled, a snapshot named lxc_update_check is taken; the previous one is replaced. If the storage cannot do snapshots, the update continues without one."
L[doc_step2]="System packages: all packages are upgraded without prompts (apt-get dist-upgrade, or apk, dnf, pacman on other systems). Configuration files you changed are kept."
L[doc_step3]="App: the community-script update runs unattended, like the \"update\" command in the container. If it would install a pre-release (beta), this step is skipped."
L[doc_step4]="Docker: in every compose project of the container \"docker compose pull\" and \"docker compose up -d\" are run. Containers started individually with \"docker run\" stay unchanged."
L[doc_step5]="Check: finally everything is checked again. Above the table the report shows the result and a link to the log."
L[doc_rollback]="To return to the state before the update if something stopped working:"
L[doc_limits]="Each step may take at most one hour (UPDATE_TIMEOUT in the config file). If a community-script asks a question during the update, step 3 fails; the log will say so."

